# Paper Global Rules

Apply this rule whenever a task uses Paper, the Paper MCP server, or Paper design artifacts.

## Core Output Default

- Unless the user explicitly says otherwise, always produce three responsive breakpoints:
  - Desktop
  - Tablet
  - Phone
- Treat this as the default completion bar for Paper design output.

## Non-Destructive Editing Policy

- Never override, mutate, or repurpose an existing design frame/artboard as the primary output.
- Always draw a fresh frame on the indicated page for new work.
- If the user asks for revisions, create a fresh version frame rather than replacing the prior frame.

## Paper MCP Preflight

Before Paper tool calls:

- Ensure Paper Desktop is open with a file active.
- If MCP connection fails, instruct the user to open/reopen Paper Desktop and retry.
- Read MCP tool schemas/descriptors before calling tools.
- Confirm the target page and intended output location before creating frames.

## Required Skills And Guidance

For Paper workflows, load and follow:

- `.cursor/skills/paper-mcp/SKILL.md` — shared preflight and tool conventions
- `.cursor/skills/paper-code-to-design/SKILL.md` — code-to-design tasks
- `.cursor/skills/paper-design-to-code/SKILL.md` — design-to-code tasks

Use the Paper MCP servers configured in this environment and their current tool descriptors as the source of truth for valid operations and parameters.

## Annotations (required for labeled variants)

Do **not** put captions, eyebrows, or agent notes inside design artboards.

Use a page-level sibling Frame named **`note`** above the artboard (same width, two-line eyebrow + instruction). Full pattern:

- `docs/design-system/paper-annotations.md`

## Coach typography in Paper (load only when needed)

If this project uses **Helvetica Neue LT Pro Extended** and new Paper text looks regular-width / Roman / `system-ui`, load:

- `docs/design-system/paper-helvetica-extended.md`

Do **not** load that doc for ordinary code typography — only for Paper MCP text that must match Extended.

If a **one-line** Helvetica label next to an icon in a button/chip looks optically high or low, load:

- `docs/design-system/helvetica-icon-optical-align.md`

Do **not** load that doc for paragraphs or multi-line copy.

## Consistency And Handoff Quality

- Maintain content parity across desktop/tablet/phone unless the user explicitly requests breakpoint-specific differences.
- Name new frames predictably using surface + breakpoint + version, for example: `Hero_Desktop_v2`.
- For each breakpoint, provide complete handoff-ready structure:
  - Layout constraints and spacing behavior
  - Typographic roles/styles
  - Token-aligned color and style usage

## Maintenance Note (Light Upkeep)

- Recheck Paper skill file paths periodically (at least quarterly) and after plugin updates.
- If Paper MCP tools or descriptors change, update the skills and this rule to match the current toolset.
- Keep examples and naming conventions current with the active project workflow.
